course: dictionary
lesson: 8773
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so the sentence around it tells you which one is right. «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes, which give them shade.» Here shade is a place out of the sun, because lions rest there to stay cool and safe. Ask: what job is the word doing in this sentence?
explain: Look at «adding white makes a tint, adding black makes a shade» in the colour sentence. A shade here is a lighter or darker version of one colour. The word is the same as before, but the clues are about paint and colour, not sunlight.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Shade your eyes» means cover your eyes from the bright sun, and «shade 3 of 4 squares» means colour in three of the four. When the swap makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Shade can be a noun or a verb. As a verb it can mean to block light from something, or to colour part of a picture or diagram. Look at the object near the word: a tree, a hat or a diagram tells you whether shade is about light or colouring.
fact: Shade is an area where sunlight is blocked, so it is cooler and darker.
fact: A shade is a lighter or darker kind of a colour, such as a shade of blue.
fact: «Shades» (informal) means sunglasses.
fact: The sun's UV is strongest around the middle of the day, roughly 11 am to 3 pm in the UK summer, so sitting in the shade then helps.
fact: To shade something means to protect it from light, or to colour in part of a picture or diagram.
exercise: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes, which give them shade.» What does shade mean here? | Sunglasses | An area where the sunlight is blocked | A darker kind of colour | *A place out of the sun, cooler and darker
exercise: «Adding white makes a tint, adding black makes a shade.» What is a shade in this sentence? | A place out of the sun | A pair of sunglasses | *A lighter or darker version of one colour | A lampshade
exercise: Ravi must shade 3 of the 4 squares in his maths diagram. What does shade mean? | To block the sunlight | *To colour in part of a diagram | Sunglasses | To make something lighter
test: «Shade your eyes from the bright sun.» What does shade mean here? | *To block light from something | A kind of colour | A lampshade | Sunglasses
test: Mia says, «I forgot my shades, the sun is strong.» What are shades? | Lampshades | Trees that give shelter | *Sunglasses | Lighter colours
exam: «Pale pigs can get sunburnt, so farmers sometimes give them shade or sun cream.» Which meaning of shade fits here? | *A place sheltered from the sun | A lighter colour of pink | To colour in a picture | A lampshade
